  "term": "startle response",
  "definition": "The startle response is an automatic, complex reaction triggered by a sudden intense stimulus. It includes withdrawing from the stimulus, tightening and bending of the muscles and limbs, blinking, and shifts in heart rate, blood pressure, and breathing.",
